    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under realistic conditions. It is designed to catch silent failures \u2014 the most dangerous class of bugs in distributed systems, where a node drops out or misbehaves but the system continues returning plausible-looking output.\n\n**Core principle:** Every check must produce a binary, reproducible pass/fail with logged evidence. A check that \"seems fine\" is a failed check.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every node in the cluster is running the exact same logical system.\n\n### 1.1 Model artifact identity\n- [ ] Compute and record a content hash (SHA-256) of model weights on **every node**, not just the coordinator. Verify all hashes match.\n- [ ] If weights are sharded across nodes (tensor/pipeline parallelism), hash each shard and verify the shard manifest matches the expected layout on every node.\n- [ ] Record tokenizer files (vocab, merges, special tokens) and hash them; verify identity across all nodes. Tokenizer drift between nodes causes silent corruption in pipeline-parallel setups.\n- [ ] Record model config (architecture, dtype, rope settings, quantization scheme) and verify byte-identical across nodes.\n- [ ] Verify quantization parameters (scales, zero-points) are identical where they are replicated, and that quantized shards load with the expected group sizes.\n\n### 1.2 Runtime and dependency identity\n- [ ] Record versions of: inference engine, framework (PyTorch/JAX/etc.), CUDA/ROCm, driver versions, NCCL/HCCL/Gloo communication library versions, and Python interpreter version on every node.\n- [ ] Verify all nodes report identical versions. Document any tolerated divergence explicitly (e.g., driver minor-version skew",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
